# The old reader is retired.  `reader.html` and `reader2.html` both existed for
# months and the site's navigation pointed at BOTH — the home page opened
# reader2, while search results and the top-nav opened reader (2026-07-30h).
# The links were repointed then, but a bookmark or an external link still
# landed on the frozen reader: no section search, no concordance-driven layer
# buttons, no book tooltips.  Redirected rather than deleted, so an old link
# still arrives somewhere useful.
#
# Cloudflare preserves the query string across a redirect and the fragment is
# kept by the browser, so an old deep link of the form
#   /reader/reader.html?q=X#VOL/<id>
# survives intact — and reader2 understands that legacy hash form (2026-07-30h).
/reader/reader.html /reader/reader2.html 301
/reader/ /reader/reader2.html 301
